<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Ottoman–Venetian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1537">1537</a>–<a href="/years/1540">1540</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Ottoman–Venetian War was fought from 1537 to 1540 between the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a>. After an Ottoman siege of Corfu failed, a Holy League fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrea-doria">Andrea Doria</a> was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayreddin-barbarossa">Hayreddin Barbarossa</a> at Preveza in 1538. In the peace of 1540 Venice gave up its last possessions in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Morea</a> and most of its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> islands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/third-ottoman-venetian-war.jpg" alt="Third Ottoman–Venetian War" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osman Nuri Pasha and Hovhannes Umed Behzad (1809–1874) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Preveza_(1538).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
